# Bot CLI in this project

This project was scaffolded with `--kind bot`: the standard MT5 compose stack plus
the files an external decision source (AI agent, python model, human script) needs.
The `qkt.config.yaml` here is what `qkt bot` reads when run from this directory —
its `risk:` block, broker profiles, and `insights:` egress all apply to bot trading.

Two ways to trade through the bot surface:

| Mode | Command shape | Risk engine | Backtestable |
|---|---|---|---|
| One-shot | `qkt bot buy ...` (no session) | venue-side only | no |
| Run session | `qkt bot session start` + same verbs | full pipeline from `qkt.config.yaml` | yes — same reports as `qkt backtest` |

## One-shot verbs (no session)

```bash
qkt bot account --json
qkt bot quote MT5:XAUUSD --json
qkt bot bars MT5:XAUUSD --tf 1h --count 100 --json
qkt bot eval "ema(21)" MT5:XAUUSD --tf 1h --json
qkt bot buy 0.01 MT5:XAUUSD --sl by:5 --tp by:10 --dry-run --json   # offline preview
qkt bot buy 0.01 MT5:XAUUSD --sl by:5 --tp by:10 --as smoke --json  # real (demo!) order
qkt bot positions --json
qkt bot close MT5:XAUUSD --all --json
```

## Run sessions — your logic, qkt's pipeline

A session is a foreground process holding the real trading pipeline (risk rules,
sizing, fills, insights identity). Your program pulls bars and pushes orders with
plain `qkt bot` verbs; the session makes them real. The same client loop runs
against a backtest or the live feed.

### Backtest an external decision loop

```bash
# 1. start the session over cached historical data (fails closed if data missing)
qkt bot session start --backtest \
  --symbols MT5:XAUUSD --tf 5m \
  --from 2025-01-01 --to 2025-06-30 \
  --identities mybrain --run demo --out runs/demo --json &

# 2. drive it — each `next` returns the next closed bar and advances the sim clock
qkt bot bars MT5:XAUUSD --count 200 --run demo --json   # prime your model (warmup history)
qkt bot next MT5:XAUUSD --run demo --json               # {"type":"bar",...} or {"type":"end"}
qkt bot buy 0.5 MT5:XAUUSD --sl by:5 --tp rr:2 --as mybrain --run demo --json
qkt bot positions --run demo --json                     # model truth at the sim cursor

# 3. finish -> the standard backtest report lands in runs/demo/
qkt bot session finish --run demo --json
ls runs/demo   # result.json trades.csv equity_global.csv pnl_components.csv report.html ...
```

Risk rules from `qkt.config.yaml` (max_daily_loss, drawdown halts, pre-trade caps)
veto orders exactly as they would a deployed strategy; rejections land in
`rejections.csv`. Every read your program made is journaled to the session's
`reads.jsonl` — the report captures what the agent saw, not just what it did.

### The same loop, live

```bash
qkt bot session start --symbols MT5:XAUUSD --tf 5m \
  --identities mybrain --run paperlive --json &
# identical client loop: next / buy / sell; `next` now blocks until a real bar closes
# positions/account stay venue truth; orders go through the pipeline's risk first
qkt bot session finish --run paperlive --json
```

### Minimal python executor

```python
import json, subprocess

def qkt(*args):
    out = subprocess.run(["qkt", "bot", *args, "--run", "demo", "--json"],
                         capture_output=True, text=True)
    return json.loads(out.stdout)

model_state = qkt("bars", "MT5:XAUUSD", "--count", "200")   # prime
while (bar := qkt("next", "MT5:XAUUSD"))["type"] != "end":
    if my_model.decide(bar) == "buy":
        qkt("buy", "0.5", "MT5:XAUUSD", "--sl", "by:5", "--tp", "rr:2", "--as", "mybrain")
```

The same script backtests (session started with `--backtest`) or trades live
(without) — that is the parity contract.

### Multiple external strategies, one session

Declare them at start (`--identities momentum,meanrev`) and tag every order with
its `--as` name. The backtest report splits per identity
(`equity_momentum.csv`, per-strategy rows in `trades.csv`); account-level risk
sees the whole session.

## qkt-insights

The compose stack ships a qkt-insights service, disabled by default behind the
`insights` compose profile (the "commented-off" service — nothing runs until you
opt in):

```bash
docker compose --profile insights up -d          # enable the dashboard
# then set insights.enabled: true in qkt.config.yaml (see the insights: block)
```

Once enabled, every bot command, order, and fill egresses with your `--as` name as
its strategy id, and session activity additionally carries `run=<run-id>` in the
payload so a whole campaign groups as one unit in the dashboard.

## Journals and state

- `state/bot/<as>/journal-*.jsonl` — every command/order/result, append-only.
- `state/bot/sessions/<run>/` — live session descriptor + `reads.jsonl`.
- Reports land wherever `--out` points (default `runs/<run-id>/`).

Full reference: https://elitekaycy.github.io/qkt/reference/bot-cli/ (qkt {{QKT_VERSION}})
